* Thu Mar 05 2020 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 2.2.0-0BX01
- Fix for critical security flaw that allowed privilege escalation due to
  account 'root-admin' not getting a password hash set on initial server
  setup. Nor was the password hash set when the admin password changed.
- Modified glue/handlers/handle_password.pl to add debugging.
- Modified glue/handlers/root_access.pl to add debugging. Identified that
  it was running our internal Base::User 'usermod', but expecting different
  return states. Added check and countermeasure to make sure that a root
  level server admin account will not have an empty password. As fallback
  it will set the hash from the 'root' account itself if need be.
- Modified perl/User.pm to fix various issues that were introduced when
  support for Jails was added. Eliminated the chance that usermod or useradd
  is run with an empty password or password hash string, which was the root
  cause of the security flaw: During initial setup and this unlucky series of
  intermingling faults the account root-admin was created by running
  useradd -p ''. Which never should have happened in first place. Additional
  steps were taken to make sure that this can't happen again.

